<script setup>
import {computed,ref} from 'vue'
const angle=ref(38);const magnitude=ref(1);const vector=computed(()=>({x:280+Math.cos(angle.value*Math.PI/180)*magnitude.value*150,y:230-Math.sin(angle.value*Math.PI/180)*magnitude.value*150}))
</script>
<template><div class="split wide-left"><div class="col"><svg viewBox="0 0 600 420" class="diagram" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative direction and magnitude in a two-dimensional projection of z"><line x1="30" y1="230" x2="575" y2="230" class="grid-lines"/><line x1="280" y1="405" x2="280" y2="20" class="grid-lines"/><circle cx="280" cy="230" r="150" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/><line x1="280" y1="230" :x2="vector.x" :y2="vector.y" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="3"/><circle :cx="vector.x" :cy="vector.y" r="7" fill="var(--blue)"/><circle cx="280" cy="230" r="4" fill="var(--ink)"/><text :x="vector.x+12" :y="vector.y-10" class="svg-value">z</text><text x="287" y="251" class="svg-label">0</text><text x="560" y="252" class="svg-label">z₁</text><text x="292" y="25" class="svg-label">z₂</text><text x="30" y="398" class="svg-label">Illustrative projection · no learned latent values</text></svg></div><div class="col"><h2>Direction and strength</h2><p class="formula">z = ‖z‖ · ẑ</p><label class="small">Direction: {{angle}}°<input v-model.number="angle" style="width:100%" type="range" min="10" max="165" aria-label="Illustrative latent direction" @keydown.stop/></label><label class="small">Magnitude: {{magnitude.toFixed(2)}}<input v-model.number="magnitude" style="width:100%" type="range" min="0" max="1.2" step="0.05" aria-label="Illustrative latent magnitude" @keydown.stop/></label><p>The report interprets direction as editing type and magnitude as strength.</p><p class="note">This is an empirical interpretation of the learned space. The decoder is nonlinear; z = 0 is not an architectural guarantee of the original image.</p><p class="small muted">A real direction/magnitude render grid requires the trained decoder and its exported images.</p></div></div></template>
